== P-9, the float identity, against live project uccixoonmbhrnyczyigt
== 22 September 2026

-- FIRST RUN. The probe refused the check.

ERROR:  42702: column reference "title" is ambiguous
DETAIL:  It could refer to either a PL/pgSQL variable or a table column.
QUERY:  not exists (
      select 1 from public.risk_alerts
       where status = 'open' and title = title and entity_type = 'escrow_invariant'
    )
CONTEXT:  PL/pgSQL function private.escrow_invariants_check() line 102 at IF
PL/pgSQL function inline_code_block line 30 at assignment

This is the bug the probe exists to find. Had the variable been called
anything the table does not also use, the condition would have been a
tautology and the deduplication would have gone silent after its first
finding, which is a check that looks like it is passing.

Fixed by replacing the body: the comparison is now on `ra.entity_id`.

