== The unit side of the same invariant: apps/web/src/lib/escrow/float.test.ts
== 22 September 2026

THE TEST WAS WATCHED FAILING BEFORE IT WAS BELIEVED. The commission
subtraction inside `floatFromLedger` was removed on purpose and the suite run:

 FAIL  src/lib/escrow/float.test.ts > holds across a full lifecycle mix, to the kobo
 FAIL  src/lib/escrow/float.test.ts > counts the commission out of the float, because a release credits the net
   AssertionError: expected 50000 to be +0
 FAIL  src/lib/escrow/float.test.ts > stays in whole kobo and never produces a fraction
   AssertionError: expected 16667 to be +0

 Test Files  1 failed (1)
      Tests  3 failed | 4 passed (7)

The subtraction was restored:

 Test Files  1 passed (1)
      Tests  7 passed (7)

Three of seven assertions are genuinely connected to the arithmetic they name,
and the identity itself is one of the three.

